@startuml GovernedLegalWorkflowComplianceTOE
title Governed legal workflow compliance extension

skinparam componentStyle rectangle

package "Current-master governed legal workflow" {
  [GovernedLegalWorkflowTOEBridgeExact] as Workflow
}

package "Existing source owners" {
  [ExpertEvidenceProductionIntegrity] as Expert
  [RealMatterReviewDecision] as Review
  [PromotionSpine] as Promotion
  [LegalDecisionDoubleProjection] as Decision
  [LegitimacyEvidenceSeparation] as Legitimacy
  [DomainPermeabilityAuthorityTransport] as Domain
  [BalabanIbrahimParetoSnowballTOEExact] as Ibrahim
  [FleetFormalGapTargetTOEExact] as Fleet
}

package "Unique compliance extension" {
  [GovernedLegalWorkflowComplianceTOEExact] as Compliance
  [GovernedLegalWorkflowComplianceTOEValidation] as Validation
}

package "Canonical TOE roots" {
  [EverythingTOESymmetryResolved369] as TOE
  [Unifier] as Unifier
  [Unified.Everything] as Unified
}

Workflow --> Compliance : canonical legal workflow handoff
Expert --> Compliance : qualification != forensic compliance
Review --> Compliance : review != claim truth
Promotion --> Compliance : missing gate -> abstain
Decision --> Compliance : official surface != fine state
Legitimacy --> Compliance : legality != legitimacy
Domain --> Compliance : vendor identity != authority
Ibrahim --> Compliance : search priority != proof
Fleet --> Compliance : 584 closed / 44 separate / 58 target

Compliance --> TOE
Compliance --> Unifier
Compliance --> Validation
TOE --> Validation
Unifier --> Validation
Compliance --> Unified
Validation --> Unified

note right of Compliance
No Actionstep ontology is created.
Actionstep-style workflow reuse uses the vendor-neutral domain transport owner.
end note

note bottom of Fleet
The fleet count is not a named gap manifest.
Per-gap dispatch remains blocked until the named manifest exists.
Equal cardinality does not create same-object identity.
end note

@enduml
